  "classification_note": "Incidence/rupture GWAS (SAH I60 / ICH I61 / PheCode 430.x) and all-cause hydrocephalus GWAS DO have downloadable sumstats, but they are NOT SAH secondary-injury endpoints (wrong estimand) and were deliberately EXCLUDED from the severity MR rather than relabelled.",
  "conclusion": "No SAH-specific severity / secondary-injury / functional-outcome GWAS (NIHSS, modified Rankin, delayed cerebral ischemia, vasospasm, hematoma volume, poor outcome after SAH) with downloadable harmonised sumstats exists on the GWAS Catalog FTP -- all such Catalog entries report summaryStatistics=NA / 404. The reviewer's 'protein -> secondary-injury MR' is therefore a data-blocked analysis awaiting a matched SAH severity GWAS.",
  "incidence_caveat": "SAH GCST90473583 / ICH GCST90473584 (cached on disk, downloadable) are INCIDENCE / rupture endpoints (ICD10 case vs control). They measure whether the vessel ruptures, NOT the post-rupture secondary-injury / severity / functional-outcome phenotype the reviewer asked for. Relabelling them as 'secondary injury' would be an estimand error; they are reported only to document that a downloadable endpoint of the WRONG estimand exists.",
  "ischemic_proxy_note": "The closest severity/outcome GWAS in the Catalog are 3-month functional outcome (modified Rankin score) after ISCHAEMIC stroke (GCST007672 / GCST007676) and hematoma volume after ICH (GCST006139 / GCST006140). All report summaryStatistics=NA and the harmonised FTP file 404s, so even these non-SAHA proxies cannot be executed. If ever available they would be a PROXY estimand (wrong vascular territory for SAH) and must not be described as SAH secondary injury."
}